@@ -7,6 +7,13 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+- **Scheduled jobs can now auto-cancel and be cancelled programmatically.** Previously a schedule could only be stopped by a human at `/agents → Scheduled jobs`, so a recurring "monitor X until it finishes" interval had no way to end itself and the model that created it had no way to stop it. Three additions close that gap:
+  - **`manage_schedule` tool** (`list` / `cancel` / `pause` / `resume`) — the programmatic counterpart to the menu, with `job_id` resolving an id or a unique name. `cancel` removes the job and aborts its in-flight run. Registered whenever scheduling is enabled and excluded from subagent tool inheritance like the other orchestration tools.
+  - **Self-cancellation** — every recurring fire's prompt is appended with a short `[scheduler]` note naming the job id and instructing the agent to end its final reply with the exact line `[schedule-complete]` once the schedule's purpose is met. The scheduler matches that marker in the run's result and removes the job. Existing jobs get the note at their next fire, so no re-creation is required.
+  - **Declarative auto-cancel** — `maxRuns` (remove after N runs) and `cancelOn` (remove when a run's result contains a substring) on `ScheduledSubagent`/`NewJobInput`, and fired one-shots are now removed once settled instead of lingering as disabled records. The `subagents:scheduled` `removed` event carries a `reason` (`manual`, `self`, `cancel-on`, `max-runs`, `one-shot`).
+  - **Cross-extension RPCs** — `subagents:rpc:schedules:list` and `subagents:rpc:schedules:cancel`, so an extension that scheduled work can stop it without a UI.
+
 ## [0.22.0] - 2026-10-13
 
 > **⚠️ Possibly breaking — background completion delivery changed ([#388](https://github.com/tintinweb/pi-subagents/pull/388)):**
