@@ -109,7 +109,13 @@ Schedule formats:
 
 When a schedule fires, the spawn runs in background and its completion notification arrives the same way as a manually-spawned background agent's — your parent agent reasons about the result the same way.
 
-Schedules are **session-scoped**: they reset on `/new` and restore on `/resume`. List and cancel via `/agents → Scheduled jobs` (creation is the `Agent` tool's job — there is no parallel manual-create wizard). Storage at `<cwd>/.pi/subagent-schedules/<sessionId>.json` with PID-based file locking for cross-instance safety.
+Schedules are **session-scoped**: they reset on `/new` and restore on `/resume`. List and cancel via `/agents → Scheduled jobs` (creation is the `Agent` tool's job — there is no parallel manual-create wizard), from the model with `manage_schedule`, or from another extension via the `subagents:rpc:schedules:list` / `subagents:rpc:schedules:cancel` RPCs. Storage at `<cwd>/.pi/subagent-schedules/<sessionId>.json` with PID-based file locking for cross-instance safety.
+
+### Managing and auto-cancelling jobs
+
+- **`manage_schedule`** — an LLM-callable tool, registered whenever scheduling is on, with `action: list | cancel | pause | resume` and a `job_id` (id or unique name). `cancel` removes the job so it never fires again and aborts an in-flight run.
+- **Self-cancel from the run** — every recurring fire's prompt is appended with a short `[scheduler]` note naming the job id and telling the agent to end its reply with the exact line `[schedule-complete]` when the schedule's purpose is achieved and no further runs are needed. The scheduler sees that marker in the run's result and removes the job (event reason `self`). This is what lets a "monitor X until it finishes" interval stop itself instead of firing forever.
+- **Declarative auto-cancel** — `ScheduledSubagent.maxRuns` (remove after N runs), `ScheduledSubagent.cancelOn` (remove when a run's result contains a substring), and one-shots (removed once settled, reason `one-shot`). These are set through `NewJobInput.max_runs` / `cancel_on`; the `subagents:scheduled` `removed` event carries the `reason` (`manual`, `self`, `cancel-on`, `max-runs`, `one-shot`).
 
 **Disable the feature entirely**: `/agents → Settings → Scheduling → disabled` removes `schedule` from the `Agent` tool spec (no LLM-context cost), hides the menu entry, and stops any active scheduler. The schema-level removal takes effect on the next pi session; the runtime kill is immediate. Re-enable from the same menu.
 
